$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2. Procedure for the Synthesis of 3-Subsituted Pyrazinium Salts
2-Substituted pyrazines were synthesized from 2-chloropyrazine with the
corresponding aryl boronic acids through Pd-catalyzed Suzuki coupling.
The substrate S1i was synthesized according to known method. 1a The
substrate S1n was synthesized using Pd(OAc)2-BuPAd2 catalyzed Suzuki
coupling. 1b The substrates S1a-d, 1c S1f-k, 1a S1l, 1d S1m, 1e and S1n
1f were known compounds. Under nitrogen atmosphere, 2-chloropyrazine (573
mg, 5.0 mmol), aryl boronic acid (6.5 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4(58 mg, 0.05 mmol),
toluene (15.0 mL), and water (15.0 mL) were successively added to a
reaction bulb. The resulted mixture was heated to 95°C for 10 min. Then,
it was cooled down to room temperature. The potassium fluoride dihydrate
(612 mg, 6.5 mmol) was added in one portion. The reaction mixture was
heated to 95 °C again. When 2-chloropyrazine was fully consumed, the
mixture was cooled down and the phases were separated. The aqueous phase
was extracted with ethyl acetate (10 mL×2). The combined organic layer
was washed with brine, dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated in
vacuo. Column chromatography of the residue on silica gel using petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate (10:1) as the eluent. The desired coupling product
S1. The yields were given in Table 1. The physical data of the new
compounds were given vide infra. product S1a, yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Chiral Piperazines via Hydrogenation of Pyrazines Activated
by Alkyl Halides
